1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:03,123
A triangle has three sides, three vertices and three

2
00:00:03,123 --> 00:00:06,098
angles. The three sides are line segments, and together

3
00:00:06,098 --> 00:00:10,900
they close the figure. A triangle also separates the

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:15,171
plane around it into an interior, a boundary and an exterior.

5
00:00:15,813 --> 00:00:18,851
How many sticks do we need to close a

6
00:00:18,851 --> 00:00:21,865
figure? One stick cannot close anything: its two ends

7
00:00:21,865 --> 00:00:25,045
are far apart. Two sticks make a V, and

8
00:00:25,045 --> 00:00:27,400
the two free ends are still open. Add a

9
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:31,079
third stick, and the ends meet. The figure closes.

10
00:00:31,079 --> 00:00:32,762
So three is the least number of line segments

11
00:00:32,762 --> 00:00:34,944
needed to make a closed figure.

12
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:38,934
The textbook calls this a triangle. A triangle is

13
00:00:38,934 --> 00:00:42,140
a simple closed figure formed by three line segments.

14
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:45,800
Simple, because the sides do not cross each other.

15
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:48,845
Closed, because the ends join up. And exactly three

16
00:00:48,845 --> 00:00:51,431
line segments: no more, and no fewer.

17
00:00:52,067 --> 00:00:54,817
Now let us name the parts. The three line

18
00:00:54,817 --> 00:00:57,753
segments are the sides of the triangle: side AB,

19
00:00:57,753 --> 00:01:01,967
side BC, and side CA. The three sides together

20
00:01:01,967 --> 00:01:04,458
form the boundary of the triangle.

21
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:07,220
The three points where the sides meet are the

22
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:10,340
vertices. Point A is one vertex, point B is

23
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:13,340
the second, and point C is the third. So

24
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:15,956
a vertex is a corner of the triangle, and

25
00:01:15,956 --> 00:01:17,811
it is not the same as a side.

26
00:01:18,427 --> 00:01:21,667
At every vertex, the two sides of the triangle

27
00:01:21,667 --> 00:01:26,427
form an angle. At vertex A we have angle

28
00:01:26,427 --> 00:01:29,287
BAC, at vertex B we have angle ABC, and

29
00:01:29,287 --> 00:01:32,071
at vertex C we have angle ACB. So the

30
00:01:32,071 --> 00:01:34,218
three vertices give three angles.

31
00:01:34,827 --> 00:01:37,571
How do we name a triangle? We use its

32
00:01:37,571 --> 00:01:42,267
three vertices. Going around the figure in order, A

33
00:01:42,267 --> 00:01:45,027
then B then C, gives the name triangle ABC.

34
00:01:45,027 --> 00:01:48,587
The same triangle can also be read as triangle

35
00:01:48,587 --> 00:01:50,058
BCA or triangle CAB.

36
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:54,768
A triangle divides the plane around it into three

37
00:01:54,768 --> 00:01:57,163
parts. Point P lies inside the triangle, so it

38
00:01:57,163 --> 00:02:00,024
is in the interior. Point Q lies on one

39
00:02:00,024 --> 00:02:03,296
of the sides, so it is on the boundary.

40
00:02:03,296 --> 00:02:05,500
Point R lies outside the triangle, so it is

41
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,851
in the exterior.

42
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:10,540
Now we can name the whole figure. The boundary

43
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:12,892
of the triangle together with its interior is called

44
00:02:12,892 --> 00:02:16,226
the triangular region. So the region is not only

45
00:02:16,226 --> 00:02:20,291
the shaded inside: it also includes the three sides themselves.

46
00:02:20,953 --> 00:02:24,669
Your turn. Four quick checks. First: name the three

47
00:02:24,669 --> 00:02:28,969
sides of triangle PQR. Second: name its three vertices.

48
00:02:28,969 --> 00:02:31,923
Third: name the angle at Q. And last of

49
00:02:31,923 --> 00:02:34,933
all: point X, point Y and point Z. Which

50
00:02:34,933 --> 00:02:38,553
of them is in the interior, which is on

51
00:02:38,553 --> 00:02:41,284
the boundary, and which is in the exterior?

52
00:02:52,187 --> 00:02:55,050
The three sides of triangle PQR are PQ, QR

53
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:59,161
and RP. Its three vertices are P, Q and

54
00:02:59,161 --> 00:03:02,867
R. The angle at Q is angle PQR, because

55
00:03:02,867 --> 00:03:06,212
the vertex Q stays in the middle. And point

56
00:03:06,212 --> 00:03:09,907
X is in the interior, point Y is on

57
00:03:09,907 --> 00:03:13,718
the boundary, and point Z is in the exterior.

58
00:03:14,187 --> 00:03:16,608
One last look. A triangle is a simple closed

59
00:03:16,608 --> 00:03:18,458
figure made from three line segments. It has three

60
00:03:18,458 --> 00:03:22,327
sides, three vertices and three angles. And its boundary

61
00:03:22,327 --> 00:03:26,662
together with its interior is the triangular region. Build

62
00:03:26,662 --> 00:03:30,787
the triangle, identify its parts, and locate the points.

63
00:03:30,787 --> 00:03:34,198
Thank you for watching, and see you in the next lesson.
